  "claim": "The historian that described Mary Turner Shaw as 'a born writer' wrote a biography about German military commander John Monash who planned the Allied attack at the Battle of Amiens in 1918.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Geoffrey Serle. Sentence: Alan Geoffrey Serle (10 March 1922 – 27 April 1998), known as Geoff, was an Australian historian, who is best known for his books on the colony of Victoria; \"The Golden Age\" (1963) and \"The Rush to be Rich\" (1971) and his biographies of John Monash, John Curtin and Robin Boyd.\nPage: John Monash. Sentence: The successful Allied attack at the Battle of Amiens on 8 August 1918, which expedited the end of the war, was planned by Monash and spearheaded by British forces including the Australian and Canadian Corps under Monash and Arthur Currie.\nPage: Mary Turner Shaw. Sentence: As well known historian Geoffrey Serle described her, she was ‘a born writer and research historian with imagination, the ability to tell a story and define and ask fundamental questions’.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Geoffrey Serle. Sentence: Alan Geoffrey Serle (10 March 1922 – 27 April 1998), known as Geoff, was an Australian historian, who is best known for his books on the colony of Victoria; \"The Golden Age\" (1963) and \"The Rush to be Rich\" (1971) and his biographies of John Monash, John Curtin and Robin Boyd.\nPage: John Monash. Sentence: The successful Allied attack at the Battle of Amiens on 8 August 1918, which expedited the end of the war, was planned by Monash and spearheaded by British forces including the Australian and Canadian Corps under Monash and Arthur Currie.\nPage: Mary Turner Shaw. Sentence: As well known historian Geoffrey Serle described her, she was ‘a born writer and research historian with imagination, the ability to tell a story and define and ask fundamental questions’.",
