        "original_id": "13d0ddd8-8b39-5051-94ea-b6c55ad242f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Geoffrey Serle, John Monash, Mary Turner Shaw, Arthur Currie, John Curtin, Robin Boyd\n- Places: Victoria\n- Events: Battle of Amiens, First World War\n- Works: The Golden Age, The Rush to be Rich\n- Topics: Australian history, biography, historical writing\n\nFacts:\n- Geoffrey Serle was born on 10 March 1922 and died on 27 April 1998.\n- Geoffrey Serle was an Australian historian best known for books on the colony of Victoria, including The Golden Age (1963) and The Rush to be Rich (1971).\n- Geoffrey Serle also wrote biographies of John Monash, John Curtin, and Robin Boyd.\n- On 8 August 1918, the successful Allied attack at the Battle of Amiens helped expedite the end of the First World War.\n- John Monash planned the Allied attack at the Battle of Amiens, and British forces including the Australian Corps under John Monash and the Canadian Corps under Arthur Currie spearheaded it.\n- Geoffrey Serle described Mary Turner Shaw as a born writer and research historian with imagination, storytelling ability, and the capacity to define and ask fundamental questions.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d65c1280-72f9-53b4-87a5-8e4db6f861c3",
        "text": "Page: Geoffrey Serle. Sentence: Alan Geoffrey Serle (10 March 1922 – 27 April 1998), known as Geoff, was an Australian historian, who is best known for his books on the colony of Victoria; \"The Golden Age\" (1963) and \"The Rush to be Rich\" (1971) and his biographies of John Monash, John Curtin and Robin Boyd.\nPage: John Monash. Sentence: The successful Allied attack at the Battle of Amiens on 8 August 1918, which expedited the end of the war, was planned by Monash and spearheaded by British forces including the Australian and Canadian Corps under Monash and Arthur Currie.\nPage: Mary Turner Shaw. Sentence: As well known historian Geoffrey Serle described her, she was ‘a born writer and research historian with imagination, the ability to tell a story and define and ask fundamental questions’.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
